-- title:
--   Two charts from a non-vanishing section of 𝒪(mε)
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a Noetherian commutative ring, let $C$ be a scheme and $c : C \to \operatorname{Spec} R$ a proper morphism that is smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, and let $\varepsilon$ be a section of $c$, that is, a morphism $\operatorname{Spec} R \to C$ together with the identity $\varepsilon \cdot c = \mathrm{id}$. Let $m \ge 1$ be a natural number and let $s$ be a morphism from the unit module to `(ε.1.ker ^ m).invModule`, the dual (internal hom into the unit) of the module attached to the $m$-th power of the kernel ideal sheaf of $\varepsilon$; assume that no point in the image of the base map of $\varepsilon$ lies in the support of `Scheme.Modules.zeroSchemeIdeal s`, the smallest ideal sheaf datum whose ideal at each affine open contains the span of the coefficients of $s$ there. Then there are opens $U, V \subseteq C$ with $U \sqcup V = \top$, with $U$ the set of points outside the image of $\varepsilon$ and $V$ the set of points outside the support of the zero-scheme ideal of $s$, and sections $f \in \Gamma(C,U)$, $g \in \Gamma(C,V)$ such that $U \cap V$ equals both the basic open of $f$ and the basic open of $g$, the restrictions of $f$ and $g$ to $U \cap V$ have product $1$, and for every affine open $W \subseteq V$ the ideal of $(\varepsilon.1.\mathrm{ker})^m$ at $W$ is generated by the restriction of $g$ to $W$.
--
--   This is the two-chart (order, or pole) presentation of a relative smooth proper curve associated with a section $\varepsilon$ and a global section of $\mathcal O(m\varepsilon)$ not vanishing along $\varepsilon$: the curve is covered by the complement of $\varepsilon$ and the complement of the zero scheme of $s$, glued along a common basic open by mutually inverse coordinates, the second coordinate cutting out $\mathcal I_\varepsilon^{\,m}$ on the second chart. It feeds [`AlgebraicGeometry.SmoothProperCurve.exists_twoChartPoleDatum_forall_finrank_of_section_invModule`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.SmoothProperCurve.exists_twoChartPoleDatum_forall_finrank_of_section_invModule), where the charts and coordinates are packaged together with rank information.
